se reduced set of transform types␀␀␀␀␀␀use-intra-dct-only␀␀␀␀␀␀Use DCT only for INTRA modes␀␀␀␀use-inter-dct-only␀␀␀␀␀␀Use DCT only for INTER modes␀␀␀␀use-intra-default-tx-only␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Use Default-transform only for INTRA modes␀␀␀␀␀␀quant-b-adapt␀␀␀Use adaptive quantize_b␀coeff-cost-upd-freq␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Update freq for coeff costs. 0: SB, 1: SB Row per Tile, 2: Tile, 3: Off␀mode-cost-upd-freq␀␀␀␀␀␀Update freq for mode costs. 0: SB, 1: SB Row per Tile, 2: Tile, 3: Off␀␀mv-cost-upd-freq␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Update freq for mv costs. 0: SB, 1: SB Row per Tile, 2: Tile, 3: Off␀␀␀␀dv-cost-upd-freq␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Update freq for dv costs. 0: SB, 1: SB Row per Tile, 2: Tile, 3: Off␀␀␀␀num-tile-groups␀Maximum number of tile groups, default is 1␀␀␀␀␀mtu-size␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀MTU size for a tile group, default is 0 (no MTU targeting), overrides maximum number of tile groups␀␀␀␀␀timing-info␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Signal timing info in the bitstream (model only works for no hidden frames, no super-res yet):␀␀partition-info-path␀␀␀␀␀Partition information read and write path␀␀␀␀␀␀␀enable-rate-guide-deltaq␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Enable rate guide deltaq (1), by default off (0). It requires --deltaq-mode=3. If turned on, it requires an input file specified by --rate-distribution-info.␀␀␀rate-distribution-info␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Rate distribution information input.It requires --enable-rate-guide-deltaq=1.␀␀␀film-grain-test␀Film grain test vectors (0: none (default), 1: test-1  2: test-2, ... 16: test-16)␀␀␀␀␀␀film-grain-table␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Path to file containing film grain parameters␀␀␀denoise-noise-level␀␀␀␀␀Amount of noise (from 0 = don't denoise, to 50)␀denoise-block-size␀␀␀␀␀␀Denoise block size (default = 32)␀␀␀␀␀␀␀enable-dnl-denoising␀␀␀␀Apply denoising to the frame being encoded when denoise-noise-level is enabled (0: false, 1: true (default))␀␀␀␀enable-ref-frame-mvs␀␀␀␀Enable temporal mv prediction (default is 1)␀␀␀␀frame-parallel␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Enable frame parallel decodability features (0: false (default), 1: true)␀␀␀␀␀␀␀error-resilient␀Enable error resilient features (0: false (default), 1: true)␀␀␀aq-mode␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Adaptive quantization mode (0: off (default), 1: variance 2: complexity, 3: cyclic refresh)␀␀␀␀␀deltaq-mode␀␀␀␀␀Delta qindex mode (0: off, 1: deltaq objective (default), 2: deltaq placeholder, 3: key frame visual quality, 4: user rating based visual quality optimization, 5: HDR video, 6: Variance Boost); --deltaq-mode=1 requires --enable-tpl-model=1␀deltaq-strength␀Deltaq strength for --deltaq-mode=4 and --deltaq-mode=6 (%)␀␀␀␀␀delta-lf-mode␀␀␀Enable delta-lf-mode (0: off (default), 1: on)␀␀frame-boost␀␀␀␀␀Enable frame periodic boost (0: off (default), 1: on)␀␀␀gf-cbr-boost␀␀␀␀Boost for Golden Frame in CBR mode (pct)␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀max-inter-rate␀␀Max P-frame bitrate (pct)␀␀␀␀␀␀␀min-gf-interval␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Min gf/arf frame interval (default 0, indicating in-built behavior)␀␀␀␀␀max-gf-interval␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Max gf/arf frame interval (default 0, indicating in-built behavior)␀␀␀␀␀gf-min-pyr-height␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Min height for GF group pyramid structure (0 (default) to 5)␀␀␀␀gf-max-pyr-height␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Maximum height for GF group pyramid structure (0 to 5 (default))␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀max-reference-frames␀␀␀␀Maximum number of reference frames allowed per frame (3 to 7 (default))␀reduced-reference-set␀␀␀Use reduced set of single and compound references (0: off (default), 1: on)␀␀␀␀␀target-seq-level-idx␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Target sequence level index. Possible values are in the form of "ABxy". AB: Operating point (OP) index, xy: Target level index for the OP. E.g. "0" means target level index 0 (2.0) for the 0th OP, "1019" means target level index 19 (6.3) for the 10th OP.␀␀min-cr␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Set minimum compression ratio. Take integer values. Default is 0. If non-zero, encoder will try to keep the compression ratio of each frame to be higher than the given value divided by 100.␀␀␀color-primaries␀Color primaries (CICP) of input content:␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀transfer-characteristics␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Transfer characteristics (CICP) of input content:␀␀␀␀␀␀␀matrix-coefficients␀␀␀␀␀Matrix coefficients (CICP) of input content:␀␀␀␀chroma-sample-position␀␀The chroma sample position when chroma 4:2:0 is signaled:␀␀␀␀␀␀␀tune-content␀␀␀␀Tune content type␀␀␀␀␀␀␀cdf-update-mode␀CDF update mode for entropy coding (0: no CDF update, 1: update CDF on all frames (default), 2: selectively update CDF on some frames)␀␀sb-size␀Superblock size to use␀␀set-tier-mask␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Set bit mask to specify which tier each of the 32 possible operating points conforms to. Bit value 0 (default): Main Tier, 1: High Tier.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀use-fixed-qp-offsets␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Controls how the encoder applies fixed QP offsets for frames at different levels of the pyramid (0: adaptively-chosen offsets from --cq-level if --fixed-qp-offsets is not provided (default), 1: fixed QP offsets, 2: no QP offsets)␀␀␀fixed-qp-offsets␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Set fixed QP offsets for frames at different levels of the pyramid. Comma-separated list of 5 offsets for keyframe, ALTREF, and 3 levels of internal alt-refs. If this option is not specified (default), offsets are adaptively chosen by the encoder.␀vbr-corpus-complexity-lap␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Set average corpus complexity per mb for single pass VBR using lap. (0..10000), default is 0␀␀␀␀fwd-kf-dist␀␀␀␀␀Set distance between forward keyframes. A value of -1 (default) means no repetitive forward keyframes.␀␀enable-tx-size-search␀␀␀Enable transform size search to find the best size for each block. If false, transforms always have the largest possible size (0: false, 1: true (default)). Ignored in non rd pick mode in real-time coding.␀␀␀loopfilter-control␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Control loop filtering (0: Loopfilter disabled for all frames, 1: Enable loopfilter for all frames (default), 2: Disable loopfilter for non-reference frames, 3: Disable loopfilter for frames with low motion)␀two-pass-input␀␀The input file for the second pass for three-pass encoding␀␀␀␀␀␀two-pass-output␀The output file for the first two passes for three-pass encoding␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀two-pass-width␀␀The width of two-pass-input␀␀␀␀␀two-pass-height␀The height of two-pass-input␀␀␀␀spf␀␀␀␀␀second-pass-log␀Log file from second pass␀␀␀␀␀␀␀auto-intra-tools-off␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Automatically turn off several intra coding tools for all intra mode; only in effect if --deltaq-mode=3␀strict-level-conformance␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀When set to 1, exit the encoder when it fails to encode to a given target level␀kf-max-pyr-height␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Maximum height of pyramid structure used for the GOP starting with a key frame (-1 to 5). When set to -1 (default), it does not have any effect. The actual maximum pyramid height will be the minimum of this value and the value of gf_max_pyr_height.␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀sb-qp-sweep␀␀␀␀␀When set to 1, enable the superblock level qp sweep for a given lambda to minimize the rdcost.␀␀enable-low-complexity-decode␀␀␀␀Enable low complexity decode (0: false (default), 1: true). This supports good-quality encoding (speed 1 to 3) for vertical videos (608p to 1080p) and horizontal videos (720p to 1080p).␀␀␀␀␀␀␀screen-detection-mode␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Screen content detection mode (1: standard (default in good quality and realtime modes), 2: anti-aliased text and graphics aware (default in all intra mode))␀␀␀validate-hbd-input␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Check that input samples are within the valid range for the chosen bit depth with high bit depth encoding (0: disabled, 1: enabled (default))␀␀␀Failed to allocate mb->winner_mode_stats␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate mb->txfm_search_info.mb_rd_record␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate mb->inter_modes_info␀Failed to allocate mb->e_mbd.seg_mask␀␀␀Failed to allocate mb->dqcoeff_buf␀␀␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate gm_data->segment_map␀Failed to allocate gm_data->motion_models[m].inliers␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate row_mt_sync->mutex_␀␀Failed to allocate row_mt_sync->cond_␀␀␀Failed to allocate row_mt_sync->num_finished_cols␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate this_tile->row_ctx␀␀␀Failed to allocate enc_row_mt->num_tile_cols_done␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate PC_TREE␀␀␀␀␀␀Failed to allocate enc_row_mt->mutex_␀␀␀F